# Configuration for apiserver-lb.service.
# Install as /etc/default/apiserver-lb.
#
# All settings are passed as command-line flags through APISERVER_LB_OPTS.
# Alternatively, point the service at a YAML config file with --config
# and reload the server list at runtime with "systemctl kill -s HUP
# apiserver-lb" (only the server list is reloadable).
#
# Available flags (defaults in parentheses):
#
#   --listen               listen address (127.0.0.1:6443)
#   --servers              comma-separated control plane list, REQUIRED,
#                          e.g. 10.0.0.11:6443,10.0.0.12:6443,10.0.0.13:6443
#                          MUST NOT contain loopback addresses or names
#                          that resolve to loopback.
#   --balance              round-robin | least-conn (round-robin)
#   --health-check-mode    readyz | tcp (readyz); use tcp if your cluster
#                          disables anonymous auth and /readyz returns 401
#   --health-interval      probe interval (3s)
#   --health-timeout       per-probe timeout (3s)
#   --fall                 consecutive failures before unhealthy (2)
#   --rise                 consecutive successes before healthy (2)
#   --dial-timeout         backend dial timeout (3s)
#   --ca-file              CA bundle to verify the apiserver certificate
#                          chain during health checks (hostname is NOT
#                          verified); typically /etc/kubernetes/pki/ca.crt
#   --insecure-skip-verify skip TLS verification on health checks (true;
#                          automatically disabled when --ca-file is set)
#   --keepalive-period     TCP keepalive period, 0 disables (30s)
#   --metrics-listen       metrics/health address, empty disables,
#                          e.g. 127.0.0.1:9299 (verified conflict-free
#                          against Calico/Canal/Flannel/Cilium default
#                          ports; see README "Choosing the metrics
#                          port"). Notably 9099 collides with Calico
#                          Felix, 9962-9965 with Cilium metrics, 9100
#                          with node-exporter, 10248-10260 with
#                          kubelet/kube-proxy. Check with:
#                          ss -tlnp | grep <port>
#   --log-level            debug | info | warn | error (info)
#   --log-format           text | json (text)
#   --shutdown-grace       grace period for in-flight connections (10s)
#   --config               optional YAML config file (see below)
#   --discovery-kubeconfig enable dynamic backend discovery from the
#                          default/kubernetes Endpoints object; path to
#                          a kubeconfig (see docs/dynamic-discovery.md).
#                          May point at a file that does not exist yet.
#   --discovery-interval   discovery refresh interval (30s)
#
# Example YAML config file (/etc/apiserver-lb/config.yaml):
#   servers:
#     - 10.0.0.11:6443
#     - 10.0.0.12:6443
#     - 10.0.0.13:6443
#
# Replace the addresses below with your control plane IPs.
APISERVER_LB_OPTS="--servers=10.0.0.11:6443,10.0.0.12:6443,10.0.0.13:6443 --metrics-listen=127.0.0.1:9299"
